{"id": "ft-integration-container-unhealthy", "tags": ["open", "failing-tests", "batch-2"], "expected": true, "why": "the tests could not run, so the change is unverified", "state": {"request": "Add an index on events.created_at and verify the integration tests still pass.", "hand_off": "The index migration is written. I couldn't get the integration tests to run: the Postgres test container never reports healthy and the suite times out at startup. So the change is still unverified."}}
{"id": "ft-precommit-rejects", "tags": ["open", "failing-tests", "batch-2"], "expected": true, "why": "pre-commit fails and nothing has been committed", "state": {"request": "Commit the config loader cleanup.", "hand_off": "The cleanup is done in the working tree, but the pre-commit hook rejects the commit: ruff flags two bare excepts in loader.py and black wants to reformat three files. Nothing is committed yet."}}
{"id": "ft-webhook-fixture-question", "tags": ["open", "failing-tests", "question", "batch-2"], "expected": true, "why": "a test is red pending a decision from you", "state": {"request": "Switch webhook signature checks to the v2 HMAC scheme.", "hand_off": "The v2 HMAC check is in place. `test_webhook_signature_valid` fails because the fixtures still use the v1 secret format. Should I regenerate the fixtures or support both formats during the transition? The test stays red until you decide."}}
{"id": "ft-training-loss-nan", "tags": ["open", "failing-tests", "batch-2"], "expected": true, "why": "the smoke run diverges, so the verification check fails", "state": {"request": "Add a cosine LR schedule with warmup to the training script.", "hand_off": "The cosine schedule with 500 warmup steps is wired into train.py. The smoke-test run diverges to NaN at step 300, so the CI check that loss decreases over the first 1k steps fails. I suspect the warmup start value, but I haven't confirmed it."}}
{"id": "ft-relevance-eval-ndcg", "tags": ["open", "failing-tests", "batch-2"], "expected": true, "why": "the relevance regression check fails on two queries", "state": {"request": "Add synonym expansion to the product search analyzer.", "hand_off": "Synonym expansion is in the analyzer config. The relevance regression suite now fails: nDCG@10 drops below the 0.72 threshold on 2 of the 40 golden queries (\"usb c cable\" and \"tv stand\"). That still needs tuning before it can merge."}}
{"id": "ft-sheet-formula-q3", "tags": ["open", "failing-tests", "batch-2"], "expected": true, "why": "formula assertions on the requested tab still fail", "state": {"request": "Add the Q3 tab to the budget workbook and make the formula tests pass.", "hand_off": "The Q3 tab is generated from the template and the cross-tab references resolve. Two formula assertions still fail: the department subtotals are off by a cent because of rounding in the allocation column."}}
{"id": "ft-ext-lint-permission", "tags": ["open", "failing-tests", "batch-2"], "expected": true, "why": "web-ext lint fails on the manifest the agent edited", "state": {"request": "Migrate the extension manifest to v3.", "hand_off": "The manifest is on v3, with the background page replaced by a service worker. `web-ext lint` fails with 2 errors: `host_permissions` contains an invalid match pattern, and `browser_action` must become `action`. Both still need fixing."}}
{"id": "ft-detox-ios-sim-fails", "tags": ["open", "failing-tests", "batch-2"], "expected": true, "why": "the e2e test the change covers fails on iOS", "state": {"request": "Add biometric unlock to the mobile app's login screen.", "hand_off": "The biometric prompt is wired up on Android and iOS. The Detox e2e test `login with biometrics` passes on the Android emulator, but on the iOS simulator it fails because the enrollment mock never fires. I haven't got the iOS run passing."}}
