{"id": "ft-log-excerpt-dedupe-last", "tags": ["open", "failing-tests", "long", "code", "batch-2"], "expected": true, "why": "the final run shown ends with a failing test", "state": {"request": "Deduplicate ingested records by content hash.", "hand_off": "Hash-based dedupe changes:\n\n- `content_hash()` normalises whitespace and key order before SHA-256.\n- The writer checks a seen-set and `record_hashes` before inserting.\n- Unique index on `record_hashes.hash`.\n\nFinal run:\n\n```\n$ pytest tests/test_ingest.py -q\n.......................F.\n_____ test_dedupe_by_hash _____\n>       assert written == 983\nE       assert 978 == 983\ntests/test_ingest.py:212: AssertionError\n1 failed, 24 passed in 2.10s\n```"}}
{"id": "ft-upbeat-buried-dry-run", "tags": ["open", "failing-tests", "long", "buried", "batch-2"], "expected": true, "why": "a migration dry-run failure sits mid-summary", "state": {"request": "Add per-tenant email uniqueness and migrate the users table.", "hand_off": "Great news, most of this landed nicely!\n\nWhat's in:\n- Unique index on (tenant_id, lower(email)).\n- Signup and invite return a friendly 409 on a duplicate.\n- 14 new unit tests, all green.\n\nOne snag: the migration dry-run on the staging snapshot fails at step 4. The index hits duplicates from 37 tenants with case-only email differences, and I haven't written that cleanup, so the migration can't run.\n\nAlso updated the API docs and changelog. Nice set of improvements!"}}
{"id": "ft-numbered-steps-release-end", "tags": ["open", "failing-tests", "long", "list", "batch-2"], "expected": true, "why": "the last step's release build fails, so no APK yet", "state": {"request": "Prepare the 3.2.0 release of the Android app: version bump, changelog, signing config and a release build.", "hand_off": "Release prep for 3.2.0:\n\n1. Bumped versionName to 3.2.0 and versionCode to 320.\n2. Wrote the changelog from merged PRs since 3.1.4.\n3. Signing config now reads environment variables.\n4. Updated ProGuard rules.\n5. Unit tests (212) and lint pass.\n6. Ran `./gradlew bundleRelease`.\n\nStep 6 is where it stops: R8 fails with `Missing class com.example.payments.TokenCallback`, which needs a keep rule I haven't worked out, so no release bundle exists yet."}}
{"id": "ft-ci-matrix-table-312", "tags": ["open", "failing-tests", "long", "list", "batch-2"], "expected": true, "why": "the Python 3.12 CI job is red on the branch", "state": {"request": "Drop the six dependency and make the library work on Python 3.10 through 3.12.", "hand_off": "Replaced every `six` import with stdlib equivalents and dropped the pin.\n\nCI matrix on the branch:\n\n| Job | Python | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| lint | 3.12 | pass |\n| test | 3.10 | pass |\n| test | 3.11 | pass |\n| test | 3.12 | FAIL (2 errors) |\n\nBoth 3.12 failures are in `tests/test_compat.py`, which imports `distutils.version.LooseVersion`, removed in 3.12. It needs to move to `packaging.version`; I haven't done that, so the branch is red on 3.12."}}
{"id": "ft-bullets-e2e-mid-reflex-tail", "tags": ["open", "failing-tests", "long", "buried", "reflex", "batch-2"], "expected": true, "why": "an e2e failure is buried before a routine reflex tail", "state": {"request": "Add 3-D Secure support to the card payment step.", "hand_off": "3-D Secure is wired into the card step:\n\n- Intents use `request_three_d_secure: automatic`.\n- A challenge modal opens on `requires_action`.\n- The e2e checkout spec fails at the 3DS step: the iframe never loads in headless Chrome and it times out. I haven't found why.\n\nRestart the dev server to pick up `PAYMENTS_3DS_ENABLED`.\n\nWhat to look for:\n- A 3DS test card shows a challenge before the order confirms.\n- Cancelling returns you to the card step."}}
{"id": "ft-several-failing-auth-list", "tags": ["open", "failing-tests", "long", "list", "batch-2"], "expected": true, "why": "three tests in the rewrite still fail", "state": {"request": "Rewrite token refresh so refresh tokens rotate on every use.", "hand_off": "The refresh rewrite is in `auth/refresh.go`: each refresh issues a new token, records its parent in `token_family`, and revokes the family on replay.\n\nRefresh suite:\n\n- `TestRefreshRotatesToken`: pass\n- `TestRefreshExpired`: FAIL (401, expected 403)\n- `TestConcurrentRefresh`: FAIL (both parallel refreshes succeed)\n- `TestReplayRevokesFamily`: FAIL (siblings stay valid)\n- `TestRevokeOnLogout`: pass\n\nThat leaves three failures to work through."}}
{"id": "ft-long-golden-render-diff", "tags": ["open", "failing-tests", "long", "code", "batch-2"], "expected": true, "why": "the golden-image test still fails after the shader change", "state": {"request": "Fix the banding in the sky gradient shader for the level editor preview.", "hand_off": "The banding came from quantising before the blend. It now blends in linear space with a blue-noise dither:\n\n```glsl\nvec3 c = mix(horizon, zenith, t);\nc += (texture(blueNoise, uv).r - 0.5) / 255.0;\n```\n\nThe preview looks smooth at 1080p and 4K. The golden-image test is still red:\n\n```\nrender_test sky_gradient_dusk ... FAIL\n  max channel diff 6 (> tolerance 2)\n```\n\nThat's more than dither explains, so I'm checking whether sRGB is applied twice."}}
