{"id": "wt-leaked-key-rotate", "tags": ["open", "waiting", "partial", "batch-2"], "expected": true, "why": "the live key must be revoked by the person before CI is updated", "state": {"request": "Deal with the API key that got committed last week.", "hand_off": "I found the key in commit `a1b2c3d` and scrubbed it from history on a local branch, not pushed yet. The key itself is still live, and only you can revoke it in the provider console. Once it's rotated, tell me the new secret's name and I'll update the CI reference and push the cleaned branch."}}
{"id": "wt-ci-matrix-py38-call", "tags": ["open", "waiting", "question", "partial", "batch-2"], "expected": true, "why": "last matrix item waits on a support-policy decision", "state": {"request": "Clean up the CI matrix.", "hand_off": "Removed the duplicate lint job and the unused macOS runner. The last item is the Python 3.8 leg: it's past end of life, but `pyproject.toml` still declares 3.8 support, so dropping it is a support-policy call. Keep it or drop it? I'll finish the matrix once you say."}}
{"id": "wt-protoc-fixed-publish-scope", "tags": ["open", "waiting", "past-tense", "partial", "batch-2"], "expected": true, "why": "earlier failure is fixed, but publishing now waits on access", "state": {"request": "Generate the client package from the protobufs and publish it.", "hand_off": "The build was failing earlier on a missing protobuf compiler; I installed protoc 25 and it's green now. The generated client is ready in `dist/`. Publishing it to the internal package index needs write access I don't have. Can you grant the CI token the publish scope, or run `npm publish` from `dist/` yourself?"}}
