{"id": "wt-adc-vref-measurement", "tags": ["open", "waiting", "question", "batch-2"], "expected": true, "why": "diagnosis needs a physical measurement only the person can take", "state": {"request": "Find out why the ADC readings are off.", "hand_off": "Every ADC channel reads about 12% high, which points at the reference voltage rather than the code. I can't measure the board from here. What does a multimeter show between VREF and GND? If it's near 3.3 V I'll go after the calibration constants; if it's lower, it's the regulator."}}
