{"id": "dc-replay-window-optional", "tags": ["done", "caveat", "offer", "batch-2"], "expected": false, "why": "the extra is explicitly optional; the check is live", "state": {"request": "Verify webhook signatures and reject unsigned calls.", "hand_off": "Signature check is live: unsigned or tampered calls get a 401. Optional, only if you ever want it: replay protection with a 5-minute timestamp window. Nothing else is needed for what you asked."}}
{"id": "dc-queued-messages-picked-up", "tags": ["done", "caveat", "terse", "past-tense", "batch-2"], "expected": false, "why": "waiting messages were drained; lag back to zero", "state": {"request": "Make the consumer ack only after the DB write commits.", "hand_off": "Consumers now ack after the write commits, so a crash mid-batch re-delivers instead of dropping. Messages that were waiting during the deploy got picked up on restart; lag is back to zero."}}
{"id": "dc-expires-in-unit-ambiguous", "tags": ["done", "caveat", "batch-2"], "expected": false, "why": "ambiguous docs resolved by testing; refresh works", "state": {"request": "Implement OAuth token refresh for the billing client.", "hand_off": "Token refresh works end to end against the provider's sandbox. Their docs never say whether `expires_in` is seconds or milliseconds, so I checked: a fresh token reported 3600 and expired an hour later, so seconds. I left a one-line comment at the parse site saying so."}}
{"id": "dc-dev-only-staging-untouched", "tags": ["done", "caveat", "batch-2"], "expected": false, "why": "request covered dev only; staging is information", "state": {"request": "Resize the dev environment's database instance with Terraform.", "hand_off": "Applied in dev, as you asked: the instance is db.r6g.large and a fresh `terraform plan` is clean. Staging has its own state file and was outside this request, so it keeps the old size; that's expected, not a leftover."}}
{"id": "dc-gzip-bottleneck-at-scale", "tags": ["done", "caveat", "batch-2"], "expected": false, "why": "a performance note about scale far beyond current data", "state": {"request": "Make the CSV export stream instead of building the file in memory.", "hand_off": "The CSV export streams now: 1M rows in 9 s with memory flat at about 40 MB. A note for the future: above roughly 20M rows the single-threaded gzip step becomes the bottleneck. Your largest table is 2M rows, so nothing to do."}}
{"id": "dc-last-write-wins-agreed", "tags": ["done", "caveat", "batch-2"], "expected": false, "why": "the limitation was agreed in the request", "state": {"request": "Add offline sync to the notes screen; last-write-wins is fine for conflicts.", "hand_off": "Offline sync for the notes screen is done. As agreed, conflicts resolve last-write-wins, so two phones editing the same note offline keep the later save. Sync tests pass on both the iOS and Android emulators."}}
{"id": "dc-discount-on-empty-cart", "tags": ["done", "caveat", "batch-2"], "expected": false, "why": "edge case is handled on purpose and tested", "state": {"request": "Let customers apply discount codes at checkout.", "hand_off": "Discount codes apply at checkout. One edge case, by design: a code entered on an empty cart is accepted and shows $0 off, so it carries over once items are added. `test_code_on_empty_cart` covers it."}}
{"id": "dc-flaky-reconnect-rerun-green", "tags": ["done", "caveat", "past-tense", "unrelated", "batch-2"], "expected": false, "why": "the failure was a known flake, rerun green", "state": {"request": "Add request IDs to the API's structured logs.", "hand_off": "Request IDs now appear on every log line and in the response header. The first CI run failed on `test_ws_reconnect`, a flaky timing test that was quarantined long before this; the rerun was green on all three jobs, and nothing in this diff touches websockets."}}
{"id": "dc-logrotate-no-errors", "tags": ["done", "caveat", "batch-2"], "expected": false, "why": "'no errors' and 'nothing left' are good news", "state": {"request": "Set up log rotation for the worker hosts.", "hand_off": "Log rotation is in place on all four worker hosts. `logrotate -d` reports no errors, nothing is left unrotated, and the old 4 GB log compressed down to 310 MB."}}
