{"id": "dn-webhook-review-offer", "tags": ["done", "clean", "offer", "reflex", "batch-2"], "expected": false, "why": "Review offer before merge is a routine reflex", "state": {"request": "Harden the payment webhook handler.", "hand_off": "The webhook handler now verifies the signature before parsing the body and rejects events older than five minutes. Tests cover a bad signature, a replayed event and a valid one, and all pass. Want me to run a review before you merge?"}}
{"id": "dn-sumifs-refund-fix", "tags": ["done", "clean", "batch-2"], "expected": false, "why": "Formula fixed and reconciled", "state": {"request": "Q3 totals in the finance sheet look too high.", "hand_off": "The Q3 total was double-counting refunds because the SUMIFS range included the adjustments column. I narrowed it to column D, and the Q3 total now matches the ledger export to the cent: $48,210.17."}}
{"id": "dn-conn-reset-not-a-bug", "tags": ["done", "clean", "question", "batch-2"], "expected": false, "why": "Answered: not a bug, nothing to change", "state": {"request": "Are the 'connection reset' lines in the API logs a bug?", "hand_off": "Not a bug. The load balancer closes idle keep-alive connections after 60 s, the client sees the reset, and it retries on a fresh socket. Every request in the sample I traced succeeded on that retry, so there's nothing to change."}}
{"id": "dn-flag-rollout-next-sprint", "tags": ["done", "clean", "batch-2"], "expected": false, "why": "\"Next sprint\" is the person's plan; flag is in", "state": {"request": "Add a feature flag for the new checkout flow.", "hand_off": "The `new_checkout` flag is in, defaults to off, and is wired through the config service with tests for both states. When you start the rollout next sprint, you can flip it per tenant from the config dashboard."}}
